            "gangue examples"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "12-05-b007",
          "type": "definition",
          "depth": 1,
          "title": "Tenor of Ore",
          "body": "Tenor is the metal content of the ore. It is generally expressed as a percentage or in parts per million (ppm) for precious metals like gold and platinum. The tenor depends on the price of the metal in the market.",
          "source": {
            "type": "textbook",
            "ref": "p.67"
          },
          "verified": true,
          "tags": [
            "tenor"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "12-05-classification",
      "title": "Classification of Ore Deposits",
      "slug": "classification-of-ore-deposits",
      "order": 2,
      "estimatedMinutes": 10,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "12-05-b008",
          "type": "list",
          "depth": 2,
          "title": "Classification by Formation Time",
          "items": [
            "**Syngenetic Ore Deposits**: Ore deposit is a rock which contains ore minerals *during* the formation of the rock. (e.g. BHQ - banded hematite quartzite, Dunite - Chromite).",
            "**Epigenetic Ore Deposits**: Rocks which contain ore minerals *after* the formation of the rock. (e.g. Vesicular basalt is epigenetic as it contains copper ore as cavity filling mineral in the cavities of the rock)."
          ],
          "source": {
            "type": "notes",
            "ref": "notes p.2"
          },
          "verified": true,
          "tags": [
            "syngenetic",
            "epigenetic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "12-05-b009",
          "type": "list",
          "depth": 1,
          "title": "Classification of Natural Resources",
          "items": [
            "**Metallic Resources**: Subdivided into Heavy Metals (Fe, Mn, Cr), Non-Ferrous (Cu, Pb, Zn, Al), and Light Metals (Mg, Be).",
            "**Non-metallic Resources**: Used in industries (Abrasive, Ceramic, Refractory, Medicine, Cement)."
          ],
          "source": {
            "type": "textbook",
            "ref": "p.68"
          },
          "verified": true,
          "tags": [
            "metallic",
            "non-metallic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "12-05-b010",
          "type": "list",
          "depth": 3,
          "title": "Geological Processes of Ore Formation",
          "items": [
            "**Igneous Processes**: Magmatic concentration (chromite), Pegmatitic (mica), Hydrothermal cavity filling/replacement.",
            "**Sedimentary Processes**: Sedimentation (coal, petroleum), Evaporation (gypsum), Residual (bauxite), Placer/Mechanical concentration (gold).",
            "**Metamorphic Processes**: Contact metasomatism, Oxidation & Supergene enrichment."
          ],
          "source": {
            "type": "notes",
            "ref": "notes p.4-10"
          },
          "verified": true,
          "tags": [
            "ore formation processes"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
