          "title": "Iron Ores Occurrence",
          "body": "Iron is the fourth most abundant element in the Earth's crust. In India, iron ores occur as sedimentary or metamorphosed sedimentary deposits (Banded Haematite Quartzite). Key deposits: Dharwar supergroup (Karnataka), Singhbhum (Jharkhand), Goa, and Ratnagiri, Sindhudurg, Gadchiroli (Maharashtra).",
