          "id": "12-05-b017",
          "type": "explanation",
          "depth": 1,
          "title": "Aluminium (Bauxite)",
          "body": "**Bauxite (Al2O3.2H2O)**: It is a residual deposit formed by weathering of aluminous rocks. Pisolitic form, dull lustre, hardness 1 to 3, sp. gr. 2.5 to 3. Found in Kolhapur, Ratnagiri, Raigad, Sindhudurg, Thane, and Palghar.",
