      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "12-05-b018",
          "type": "explanation",
          "depth": 1,
          "title": "Radioactive Minerals (Monazite)",
          "body": "Monazite (Ce, La, Th, Nd, Y)PO4 is the most abundant radioactive mineral, found mainly as beach sand placers in Kerala and Tamil Nadu. It is yellowish brown, hardness 5, sp. gr. 5. Important source of Thorium and rare Earths.",
          "source": {
            "type": "textbook",
            "ref": "p.72"
          },
          "verified": true,
          "tags": [
            "radioactive",
            "monazite"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "12-05-b019",
          "type": "list",
          "depth": 2,
          "title": "Fuel Industry",
          "items": [
            "**Coal**: Formed by sedimentation/decomposition of vegetable matter. Varieties: Peat -> Lignite -> Bituminous -> Anthracite (best variety).",
            "**Petroleum**: Organic origin from shallow marine sediments.",
            "**Unconventional Resources**: Coal Bed Methane (CBM), Shale Gas, Gas Hydrates."
          ],
          "source": {
            "type": "textbook",
            "ref": "p.72-73"
          },
          "verified": true,
          "tags": [
            "coal",
            "petroleum",
            "unconventional"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "12-05-b020",
          "type": "list",
          "depth": 2,
          "title": "Other Industrial Minerals",
          "items": [
            "**Cement Industry**: Uses Limestone and Gypsum (CaSO4.2H2O). Gypsum is added to prevent rapid hardening of Portland cement.",
            "**Abrasive Industry**: Diamond (hardness 10), Corundum (Al2O3, hardness 9), Garnet, Quartz. High hardness minerals used for cutting/polishing.",
            "**Ceramic Industry**: Uses Kaolin (Al2Si2O5(OH)4) and Feldspars (Orthoclase, Plagioclase).",
            "**Refractory Industry**: Uses minerals that withstand >1500\u00b0C without fusing. Examples: Kyanite (Al2SiO5), Bauxite, Zircon."
          ],
          "source": {
            "type": "textbook",
            "ref": "p.74-78"
          },
          "verified": true,
          "tags": [
            "cement",
            "abrasive",
            "ceramic",
            "refractory"
